+# Blocked: September reconciliation cannot be produced
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` fails with:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+`recon_2026-09.json` and the September net difference cannot be produced from the
+data available in this repository.
+
+## Why
+
+`reconcile.py` reconciles two exports per month:
+
+- `exports/ledger_<month>.csv` (general ledger)
+- `exports/bank_<month>.csv` (bank statement)
+
+The repository contains `exports/bank_2026-09.csv`, but the matching
+`exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` does not exist. Only the August ledger
+(`exports/ledger_2026-08.csv`) is present.
+
+The net difference is defined as the bank total minus the ledger total. Without
+the September ledger there is no ledger total to subtract, and the
+`missing_in_bank` / `amount_mismatch` categories cannot be determined either.
+Running the reconciliation against the bank file alone would silently report
+every bank line as `missing_in_ledger` and would misstate the net difference, so
+no September output was generated.
+
+## What is needed to unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` (same schema as the August export:
+`id,date,ref,amount`). Once it is in place, run:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+No code changes are required — the matching logic is implemented and tested.
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py` per its docstring: matches by
+  `ref`, separates `matched`, `amount_mismatch`, `missing_in_bank`,
+  `missing_in_ledger`, and computes `net_difference` as bank total minus ledger
+  total formatted to two decimals.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v test_reconcile` passes (2/2 tests).
+- End-to-end sanity check on the available August data succeeded
+  (`recon_2026-08.json`: net difference `-19.59`, 3 matched, 1 amount mismatch,
+  1 missing in bank, 1 missing in ledger); the temporary output was removed.
+- September reconciliation attempted and confirmed blocked for the reason above.
